{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1150250-effects-of-strange-blood-potency-level","id":1150250,"title":"Effects of strange blood potency level","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-16T18:40:32-07:00","id":1150250,"title":"Effects of strange blood potency level","content":"Does having an unusual blood potency level have any additional effects. What would happen if a vampire had it's blood potency reduced, even temporarily, to zero? Likewise what would happen if a ghoul had, even temporarily, had it's blood potency increased to one or more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18291-unrepentantweed","name":"Unrepentantweed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T18:44:30-07:00","id":1150251,"title":"","content":"If an effect would reduce a vampires blood potency to zero they become a revenant. That's in the book somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T09:45:42-07:00","id":1150384,"title":"","content":"OTOH, a ghoul with BP &gt; 0 would simply have better-performing Disciplines and a meaningful resistance attribute. (Oh, and a better chance of rising when killed as a revenant? Sure, why not!)<br /> <br /> There's some confusion between revenants and ghouls. The former are failed vampire embraces--the curse run amuck, so to speak. (Versus highly successful embraces that wreck the human side... i.e. draugr.) The latter are still fully human, but infected by the curse--they will (sometimes) transition to revenants once sufficiently &quot;dead&quot; enough for the curse to overwhelm the living human body.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T09:58:42-07:00","id":1150387,"title":"","content":"Strictly speaking at blood potency 1 the ghoul would get a full 10 point blood pool and start taking light damage from sunlight. Except they haven't got a humanity score so I'm not sure how much. Call it 10, Maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T12:42:09-07:00","id":1150419,"title":"","content":"Assuming we're dealing purely with the application of a BP value, I'd be inclined to rule it like the werewolf Tell:Primal Instincts, which ONLY enables pack tactics and provides a resistance attribute.<br /> <br /> Now yes, a ghoul with BP1 could raise it through experience and/or time. And if embraced or falling into revenant-hood you could argue they then start &gt; BP1/BP0. This is the stuff of interesting stories, is all.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T14:30:04-07:00","id":1151478,"title":"","content":"Ghouls with a Blood Potency higher than 0 don't exist.<br /> <br /> A vampire cannot have a Blood Potency lower than 1 (otherwise he'd be a Revenant or simply perish)<br /> <br /> The rules love you, don't abuse them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T06:38:04-07:00","id":1151631,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">There are two disciplines that grant the ability to temporarily raise the blood potency of the user. The first is the third level of the path of blood, Blood of Potency which temporarily increase Blood Potency. The other discipline, Internal Athanor, is part of Blut Alchemie which can raise the Blood Potency perhaps for quite longer.</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Given how a </span></span></b>revenant<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> undergoes a state change when it devours the blood and soul of a vampire to increase its Blood Potency I asked if like things would happen to ghouls. </span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">One view is that a ghoul increasing its blood potency gains only the benefits listed in the chart. Increasing the amount of vitae, the amount that can be spend per round and increasing supernatural tolerance. This is the position that I am inclined to take, but I figured I would ask and see if there might be other changes to account for.</span></span></b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18291-unrepentantweed","name":"Unrepentantweed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T15:40:20-07:00","id":1152317,"title":"","content":"Blood Sorcery Sacraments and Blasphemies rules also allow a master of the Transmutation theme to manipulate BP, if you use that system.<br /> Your proposal seems entirely reasonable, though if it were me, I would also have a chance of strange/bad things happening when monkeying around outside of conventional norms. The first time would go according to plan but try it again and you may have a great story/plot of how to fix what or whoever was broken in the attempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 10-23-2017, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}